# SWARM STATE — 2026-08-19 snapshot

File: openOODA/audit/swarm_state_2026_08_19.oot

Logline: durable record of which agent owns which lane on the openOODA
  project as of 2026-08-19, with file:line evidence and a next-action
  per lane. C emit + gcc remains the product path.
Setup: Phase 0 inventory (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot) was taken
  before the repair pass. This file is the post-dispatch state
  that anchors 20 sub-agents. No bash was run; no file outside
  audit/ was edited. Counts of audit/ files are taken from the
  survey note carried in the user dispatch, not from a glob.
  Read alongside: audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot (older), and the
  three compiler phalanx rollups: audit/wasm_phalanx.oot,
  audit/plan_llvm_phalanx.oot, audit/x86_phalanx.oot.
  Library ground truth: audit/library_status.oot (door + 22
  siblings).
Beats:
  §1  Lane-by-lane ownership and recent activity
  §2  Cross-lane dependencies
  §3  In-flight risks where the swarm state shows bugs/dead-ends
  §4  Recommendation per lane
  §5  Evidence index

