## §2. Cross-lane dependencies

  Library → compiler (forward dep, no work this cycle)
    Library needs new emit features: import+call gcc, pub fn simple
    args, emit-c heap/abort and slist OOB, c_emit unexpected
    SEMI/RBRACE, Result[List[T]] and nested Result/Option.
    (audit/library_status.oot:13-19)
    These are blocked on emit-c, which the compiler lane owns. The
    library cannot advance them unilaterally.

  Runtime → compiler (lockstep)
    The runtime owner is on WASM runtime (chs_rt_wasm.c,
    chs_rt_wasm_print.c). The compiler is on the WASM emit loop-6
    phalanx. They are coupled: the compiler emits a WASI import
    (wasi_snapshot_preview1 / fd_write) and the runtime supplies the
    body. (audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:29-30)
    RT role file: chs_rt_wasm_print.c, prototype in
    c_emit_preamble.oo. (audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:46-50)
    If WASM emit loop-6 closes, runtime can move to chs_rt_win32_*.c.
    That move is blocked on the compiler closing loop-6.

  Library → runtime (tied to Landlock)
    Landlock is named as a real Linux jail on the runtime side
    (chs_rt_landlock.c) and as the policy surface on the std side
    (sec/sys/landlock_engine.oo).
    (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:39, 50-58)
    A change to runtime Landlock forces a std policy review, and
    vice versa. The M172 split is sandbox plumbing, not
    Windows-bound. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:60)

  CLI → compiler (read-only product path)
    CLI consumes the compiler as a black box. `ooda launch`,
    `ooda add`, `ooda search` are product paths.
    (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:71)
    CLI smokes the wasm, x86, and llvm lanes but does not own
    emits. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:73-75)

  Install → CLI, compiler, runtime (Phase 4 Windows only)
    install_win.oo is the only Windows file plan names in install/.
    It depends on the compiler tree having a Windows emit, the
    runtime having chs_rt_win32_*.c, and the CLI adding a Windows
    install path. (audit/win_compiler_plan.oot section 1 Phase 4,
    per audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:77, 90-94)
    install_win.oo is parked; the install lane is QUIET.

  Process → all other lanes (today)
    This session is the lane that produces 19 sibling .oot files
    in audit/ (one per other sub-agent). It does not own compiler,
    runtime, library, cli, or install code. Read-only evidence
    lane.

## §3. In-flight risks

  R1. LLVM INT proof table blank.
      Phase 1-3 smokes PASSED (open68_cold_hello_smoke.oo,
      open68_main_check_smoke.oo, open68_cmds_floor_smoke.oo,
      open68_match_expr_smoke.oo).
      (audit/plan_llvm_phalanx.oot:37-41)
      The INT proof table is blank in the rollup. INT owns smokes
      and C path. (audit/plan_llvm_phalanx.oot:27, 41-42)
      Risk: SHIPPED.oot rows that cite LLVM proof are claims, not
      evidence, until INT writes the table.

  R2. x86 INT proof also blank; 8 of 12 x86 role files missing.
      x86_phalanx.oot lists 12 roles (DE1, DE2, RT, PV1, PV2, SEC,
      MEM, INT, HARN, HYG, DOCS, COORD).
      (audit/x86_phalanx.oot:91-115)
      Survey reports only 4 audit/ files exist for x86; the other
      8 are untracked. x86_int.oot is one of the missing.
      (audit/x86_phalanx.oot:103-104)
      Risk: Cycle B harvest is on disk but not proved. Next five
      items named in handoff (SysV %rdx, mut locals, while loops,
      Int one-arg + decimal write, runtime concat overflow) are
      unproved. (audit/x86_phalanx.oot:190-192)

  R3. WASM INT proof depends on emit-wasm rebuild.
      wasm_phalanx.oot section 5 requires `./oodac/oodac emit-wasm
      fixtures/wasm_print_hi.oo > /tmp/hi.wasm`.
      (audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:83-85)
      "Rebuild only if you own oodac/*.oo or runtime and you must
      run emit." Three rebuilds racing is forbidden.
      (audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:86-87)
      Risk: a process-lane audit agent has no emit rights. INT
      evidence must come from the compiler owner.

  R4. Library BLOCKED top row: import+call gcc.
      "import+call gcc (dot vs arrow, Result cells, decls)" is the
      first BLOCKED need. (audit/library_status.oot:14)
      1572 BLOCKED files out of 4476. (audit/library_status.oot:7)
      Risk: BLOCKED cannot shrink without compiler emit-c
      improvements. Library cert is far from done.

  R5. Runtime has no Windows shim owner.
      Landlock and rlimit are the two POSIX-isms named for Windows
      port. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:41)
      chs_rt_win32_*.c does not exist. The runtime owner is on
      WASM today. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:43)
      Risk: Windows lane Phase 2 cannot start until the runtime
      owner names a Windows sub-lane.

  R6. Compiler tree has overlapping owners.
      agy is on libraries and oodac (ooda/oodac/ + ooda/std/).
      (user dispatch, 2026-08-19)
      A co-agent is on WASM loop-6, x86 Cycle B, and LLVM match
      repair. Both edit oodac/*.oo. (audit/x86_phalanx.oot:31,
      86-87)
      Risk: oodac/oodac is the shared product binary. A foreign
      rebuild overwrites it. The x86 overlay pin is the only
      mitigation on disk. (audit/x86_phalanx.oot:26-30)

  R7. CLI and install lanes are unowned.
      No current diff is visible. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:75,
      92)
      install_win.oo and any Windows CLI variant are parked.
      Risk: Windows lane Phase 4 has no agent.

## §4. Recommendation per lane

  compiler
    Sequence: close WASM loop-6 phalanx first, then x86 Cycle B
    prove, then LLVM INT fill. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:115-118;
    audit/x86_phalanx.oot:55)
    Today: the compiler owner is on three emits at once. Pick one
    to finish. WASM loop-6 is the only one with a frozen API
    (audit/wasm_phalanx.oot:17-30); close that and the runtime
    can move off WASM lockstep.

  runtime
    After compiler closes WASM loop-6, start chs_rt_win32_*.c
    shims. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:118-120)
    Landlock and rlimit are the two POSIX-isms named. Do not
    start until the compiler names a Windows emit.

  library
    Continue M172 split. Landlock policy surface ties to runtime
    Landlock. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:58)
    BLOCKED top rows (import+call gcc, pub fn simple args) are
    blocked on compiler emit-c. Surface the BLOCKED counts but
    do not promise a shrink. (audit/library_status.oot:13-19)

  cli
    Quiet. No current diff. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:75)
    If a Windows CLI variant is needed, it can start today; the
    CLI tree is the smallest Windows touch.
    (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:77)

  install
    Quiet. install_xdg.oo is the active path.
    (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:90)
    install_win.oo can start now; the install lane has no
    in-flight diff. (audit/win_swarm_inventory.oot:94)

  process (this lane)
    Produce the 19 sibling audit/ .oot files. Cite file:line for
    every claim. Do not edit any code file. Do not run shell.

